# The DuckDB releases moraine builds a loadable extension for, newest
# first. One release per line; anything after the version is a
# `<submodule>=<commit>` pin, and only the first line carries them.
#
# The first line is the *primary* pin: the version both submodules sit on,
# the CLI `cargo xtask e2e` downloads, and the one the e2e suite proves
# the DuckLake chain against. Every other line is built and published by
# CI, which checks DuckDB out by tag and never touches the submodules.
#
# Why a list rather than a single pin: a C++-ABI extension carries the
# exact DuckDB version string in its metadata footer, and DuckDB refuses
# any whose string differs — patch releases included
# (`ParsedExtensionMetaData::GetInvalidMetadataError`). A user on one
# patch release cannot load another's build, so "supporting a series"
# means building each release in it separately.
#
# Bumping: `cargo xtask bump-duckdb <version>` writes this file and every
# other place naming the version, then `cargo xtask check-pins` fails until
# they all agree. Dropping an old line only stops future releases from
# carrying it; published assets stay.
#
# The current pin is a development revision: DuckDB 2.0 has no tag and no
# release assets, so there is no CLI to download and nothing to publish
# against. The version string is the one both the local build and CI stamp
# onto the checkout the `duckdb` submodule pins, and the CLI the e2e suites
# run is the one that build produces.
